{"metadata":{"name":"Sunan Abu Dawud","section":{"2":{"eng-name":"Prayer (Kitab Al-Salat)","ara-name":"كتاب الصلاة"}},"section_detail":{"2":{"hadithnumber_first":391,"hadithnumber_last":1160,"arabicnumber_first":391,"arabicnumber_last":1160}}},"hadiths":[{"hadithnumber":508,"arabicnumber":508,"text":"Rapporté par Anas : Bilal a reçu l’ordre de prononcer l’Adhan en répétant chaque phrase deux fois, et l’IQAMAH en ne répétant chaque phrase qu’une seule fois. Hammam a ajouté dans sa version : « sauf pour l’IQAMAH »","grades":[{"name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih Bukhari (605) Sahih Muslim (378)"}],"reference":{"book":2,"hadith":118},"chapter":{"id":29,"ara-name":"باب فِي الإِقَامَةِ","eng-name":"The Iqamah","isFirstHadith":true}}]}